topic: ~water_keywords()

# Pepper for the demo (15 Nov): two questions that work every time, coded here, plus hello and goodbye.
# Any sentence containing one of the words triggers the rule. The answers to the two questions come live from
# AquaMaa (the sensor's current reading and what it means); hello and goodbye are said as written.

concept:(hello) [hello hi hey "good morning" "good afternoon" "good evening" salam]
concept:(bye) [thanks "thank you" bye goodbye]

u:({*} ~hello {*}) Hello, I am AquaMaa. Qatar's wells can't speak, so I give them a voice. I watch every sensor live, and I tell you what the water means and what to do. Ask me what the salinity is now, or if the water is safe to drink.

u:({*} [temperature temperatures hot cold warm degrees] {*}) ^execute(ask, now:temperature)

u:({*} [drink drinking drinkable potable safe] {*}) Let me check the sensor. ^execute(ask, Is the water right now suitable for drinking)

u:({*} [salt salty saltiness salinity TDS "T D S" quality reading sensor water] {*}) Let me check the sensor. ^execute(ask, What is the salinity of the water right now)

u:({*} ~bye {*}) You are welcome. I will keep watching the wells. Goodbye!
